{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/962676-the-knell-a-cofd-game-for-a-single-player","id":962676,"title":"The Knell, a CofD game for a single player.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T21:03:37-07:00","id":962676,"title":"The Knell, a CofD game for a single player.","content":"Here is the Premise<br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:32px\"><u>The Knell</u></span>[/FONT]</span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]One day you heard it, everyone did. The sound was like a chime, mixed with the singing of whales. It was a global event that scientist, conspiracy theorist, and religious leaders all had a theory for. But nobody thought it was a good thing, and everyone turned out to be right. First weather patterns began to change. Storms became more common, and animals behaved strangely, often migrating to distant locations, or even committing mass suicide. It affected people too, both in similar ways, and in stranger ones.[/FONT]</span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]The Knell hit some people harder than others. First they began to forget things, like their co workers names, then bigger things, like their own names or their children\u2019s faces. Some forget how to feed themselves, or even how to breath. But the worst seem to remember things that cannot be comprended by others. These people speak in nonsense riddles, and unknown languages. So far 30% of the global population has been affected. Those who are have been dubbed the lost, or the mad, depending on their affliction.[/FONT]</span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\">[FONT=&quot;]For most, the Knell seems not to affect them much at all. They hear it on the edge of their hearing, even in soundproof environments. Eventually most people learn to just tune it out, except when it gets loud, and people began to panic.[/FONT]</span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;\"><i>It has been two years now, and the Knell hasn\u2019t stopped Kneeling. Suburbs are abandoned, business stand empty, governments are running at minimum capacity, and life goes on. Everyone has lost somebody. But you still have to go to work. You are after all, a Ranger. Thats what they started calling those in your line of work. You enforce martial law, search for the lost in the forgotten suburbs, and hunt down the mad, when they do something more than just babble incoherently, and break up the cults, that threaten to tear down what's left of society. You\u2019ve seen things. Things that shouldn\u2019t be, or things that just shouldn\u2019t be possible, but you live in impossible times.</i><br /> <br /> This is a game I want to run for my Storyteller/brother. He doesn't get to play that much since he always GM's in pretty much any game our group plays. I want to reveal mysteries over time, but this is all I got so far. Are their any cool ideas any of you can think to add to this? Possible theories of whats going on, or how I could evolve the story? Any feed back could help.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}